  "ground_truth": "on 20 July 2009",
  "final_output": "The first bank in India that was established to serve rural areas with basic banking and financial services was the **Punjab National Bank (Punjab National Bank Rural Bank)**, but more accurately, the **State Bank of India (SBI)** played a pivotal role in rural banking through its rural branch network.\n\nHowever, the first dedicated rural bank in India was the **Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)**, which were established in **1975** under the Banking Regulation Act. These banks were created specifically to provide banking and financial services to rural and underserved areas.\n\nThus, the first bank established as part of an organization serving rural areas of India with basic banking and financial services was the **first Regional Rural Bank (RRB)**, which came into existence in **1975**.\n\n**Final Answer: 1975**.",
